image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=256&amp;q=75 256w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w" src="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoin-images.coingecko.com%2Fcoins%2Fimages%2F279%2Flarge%2Fethereum.png%3F1696501628&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75"/><div class="flex items-baseline gap-1 lg:gap-2 min-w-0"><span class="text-xs lg:text-base font-bold uppercase leading-none text-shades-almost-black">ETH</span><span class="text-xs lg:text-base font-bold leading-none text-shades-mid">$2,487</span><span class="text-xs lg:text-base font-bold leading-none text-alerts-100">(<!-- -->-2.88%<!-- -->)</span></div></div></a></div></div><div class="order-3 mt-4 flex flex-col md:mt-0"><h1 class="m-0 mb-l font-semibold text-2xl md:text-[32px] md:font-bold leading-tight md:leading-[105%] tracking-tight text-shades-almost-black">After 10 Years, Ross Ulbricht Speaks Out: ‘Bitcoin Doesn’t Work Without Freedom’</h1></div><div class="order-4"><div class="flex items-center px-4 py-3 md:px-4.5 md:py-3.5 mb-5 rounded-sm bg-primary-100/20 text-shades-almost-black"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="size-6 min-w-6 mr-3" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image/?url=%2Fimages%2Fuploads%2Finfo-icon.svg&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image/?url=%2Fimages%2Fuploads%2Finfo-icon.svg&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image/?url=%2Fimages%2Fuploads%2Finfo-icon.svg&amp;w=48&amp;q=75"/><p class="m-0 text-sm leading-normal font-medium">This article was published more than a year ago. Some information may no longer be current.</p></div></div><div class="order-8 md:order-5 article__body leading-text"><p><strong>Ross Ulbricht delivered his first live public speech on May 29 since being granted a full presidential pardon by Donald Trump earlier this year.</strong></p></div><div class="order-6 mb-4 md:order-6"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3 lg:flex-row lg:gap-4 lg:justify-between lg:items-end"><div><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--></div><div class="flex flex-row gap-4 lg:ml-auto items-start"><div class="flex flex-col items-start lg:items-end gap-2"><span class="text-sm text-shades-semi-dark font-medium">WRITTEN BY</span><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><img alt="Jamie Redman" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="size-8 object-cover" style="color:transparent" src="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/jamie.png"/><a class="font-medium text-sm leading-snug text-shades-black md:uppercase" href="/author/jamie-redman/">Jamie Redman</a></div></div><div class="w-px h-15 bg-shades-semi-light"></div><div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-1"><span class="text-sm text-shades-semi-dark font-medium">SHARE</span></div></div></div></div><time dateTime="2025-05-30T14:30:27.000Z" class="order-7 mb-4 text-sm md:hidden"><span class="font-medium text-[#818085]">Published:<!-- --> </span><span class="font-medium text-shades-almost-black">May 30, 2025, 10:30 AM EDT</span></time><div class="order-5 md:order-7"><div class="relative -mx-4 mb-6 overflow-hidden md:mx-0"><img alt="After 10 Years, Ross Ulbricht Speaks Out: ‘Bitcoin Doesn’t Work Without Freedom’" fetchPriority="high" width="1200" height="675" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-full h-auto object-cover block md:rounded-lg " style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 1200px" srcSet="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w" src="/_next/image/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fstatic.news.bitcoin.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2Fhhhooppp.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="order-9 md:order-8"><div class="article__body overflow-x-hidden"><h2>Silk Road Creator Ross Ulbricht Delivers First Live Speech Following Trump Pardon</h2> <p>Standing before a live audience on stage in Las Vegas at Bitcoin 2025, <a href="/bidding-begins-on-ross-ulbrichts-pre-arrest-and-prison-mementos-as-he-embarks-on-new-chapter/">Ross Ulbricht</a> marked a dramatic turn in his life story, addressing the crowd on the exact date—May 29—that a federal judge sentenced him to two life terms plus 40 years without parole a decade ago.</p> <p>Ulbricht, the creator of the Silk Road marketplace, was freed earlier this year after President Donald Trump <a href="/promise-fulfilled-president-trump-issues-full-pardon-to-silk-road-creator-ross-ulbricht/">issued a full pardon</a> shortly following his inauguration. The case, which sparked long-standing debate about sentencing and digital liberty, had kept Ulbricht behind bars since 2013.</p> <p>“I’m free, and it’s because of you. You made this moment possible,” Ulbricht told attendees, thanking supporters who had advocated for his release over the years. His remarks, made during his Bitcoin 2025 speech, highlighted themes of “freedom, decentralization, and unity”—values he linked closely with Bitcoin’s founding principles.</p> <p>In his speech, Ulbricht spoke candidly about the years he spent in prison and the challenges of adapting to rapid technological change since his release. “I effectively went into a time capsule in 2013. And now I’m coming out like Rip Van Winkle,” he said. He described never having seen a drone or experienced virtual reality before his release and noted the explosion in cryptocurrency adoption since his incarceration.</p> <p>Referencing Bitcoin’s evolution, Ulbricht said, “When I launched Silk Road, buying a whole bitcoin would set you back less than a dollar. Pocket change. Can you imagine that?” He added:</p> <blockquote><p>Now, they’re worth over $100,000 each.</p></blockquote> <p>Ulbricht also emphasized the philosophical underpinnings of Bitcoin, saying, “Bitcoin doesn’t work without freedom. Bitcoin’s power comes from the fact that any one of us can mine if we choose to.” He continued:</p> <blockquote><p>We are all on equal footing with Bitcoin. With Bitcoin, we are all free.</p></blockquote> <div id="custom_html-59" class="widget_text td_block_template_1 widget widget_custom_html"><div class="textwidget custom-html-widget"> <div class="relative z-[1] max-w-full mx-auto mt-l mb-l rounded-sm [&amp;_iframe]:block [&amp;_iframe]:mx-auto [&amp;_iframe]:rounded-sm [&amp;_iframe]:!max-w-full [&amp;_iframe]:border-none [&amp;_iframe]:bg-transparent [&amp;_iframe]:overflow-hidden [&amp;_iframe]:[backface-visibility:hidden] [&amp;_iframe]:[transform:scale(1)]" style="width:100%;max-width:300px;aspect-ratio:300/250"></div> </div></div> <p>The crowd responded with sustained applause, reflecting Ulbricht’s symbolic status in parts of the cryptocurrency community. President Trump’s pardon of Ulbricht was one of his first high-profile clemency decisions following his return to office. The move was celebrated among libertarian circles and crypto advocates. In addition to his speech, Ulbricht raised around 16 BTC worth $1.69 million with his pre-<span style="font-weight:400">arrest gear and prison memento <a href="https://scarce.city/collections/b25-ross-ulbricht-collection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">auction</a>. </span></p> <p>In closing, Ulbricht urged the crowd to remain committed to the principles that had shaped both his case and the broader crypto movement. “Freedom, decentralization, unity,” he said. “Stay true to these principles—and the future is ours.”</p></div></div><div class="order-11 md:order-10 my-l"><!--$?--><template id="B:0"></template><!--/$--></div><div class="order-13 my-l md:hidden"><!--$?--><template id="B:1"></template><!--/$--></div><div class="order-last"></div></article></main><aside class="post-layout-sidebar"><div class="flex flex-col"><div class="mt-l min-[768px]:h-[520px] min-[768px]:overflow-hidden"><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--></div><!--$?--><template id="B:2"></template><div class="flex flex-col gap-m"><div class="flex gap-s"><div class="h-[68px] w-[68px] shrink-0 animate-pulse rounded-sm bg-surface-muted"></div><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-center gap-xs"><div class="h-[14px] w-3/4 animate-pulse rounded bg-surface-muted"></div><div class="h-[14px] w-1/2 animate-pulse rounded bg-surface-muted"></div></div></div><div class="flex gap-s"><div class="h-[68px] w-[68px] shrink-0 animate-pulse rounded-sm bg-surface-muted"></div><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-center gap-xs"><div class="h-[14px] w-3/4 animate-pulse rounded bg-surface-muted"></div><div class="h-[14px] w-1/2 animate-pulse rounded bg-surface-m